sec.p:
Based on the tree model, XGBoost uses multi-thread parallel computing to improve the convergence speed, fits the data by gradient boosting, and uses tree pruning strategy and regularization technology to prevent overfitting and reduce the influence of noise data. This method not only improves the prediction accuracy, but also is more suitable for high-dimensional and small sample data, and has been widely used in many fields21. Therefore, in view of the high-dimensional and small sample data of mine water inrush, this study uses XGBoost as the benchmark model to carry out mine water inrush source identification research, and its objective function \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
